 @coolmemesbudd  No you're wrong because you said the 4090 will be the bottleneck well BEFORE meeting any 4K240hz displays (they are already available btw). That's not the case since the most common refresh rates at 4K below 240hz are 120hz and 144hz, and both absolutely bottleneck the 4090.

There's no honest reason to limit it to native rendering only, DLSS image reconstruction set to Quality at 4K often produces a superior image than native 4K + TAA and DLSS3 AI generated frames look indistinguishable in motion at these high fps counts, so you'd absolutely want to enable the full package, and in doing so unlock even more performance headroom.

This is a card that should be targeting 8K120 to avoid CPU bottlenecks, with DLSS 3 set to the required level. At 8K, just Performance DLSS is enough to match native rendering, because image reconstruction improves the more data it has to work with. Balanced and Quality would exceed native rendering at resolving fine detail while running at a fraction the performance cost, it is remarkable technology.

